E[X] = Σ pᵢxᵢ. Worked: Offer A is certain $92,000. Offer B is $100,000 with probability 0.8 (falls through otherwise, $0). EV(B) = 0.8 × 100,000 = **$80,000** < $92,000 — the certain offer wins on expectation. Caveat: EV ignores risk tolerance and ruin (a $0 outcome may be unacceptable regardless of EV). Use EV to compare gambles, then apply your personal ruin constraint.

