Sample offers ($k): [78, 82, 85, 88, 92, 95, 110, 250]. Mean = **$110.0k**; median = **$90.0k**. One $250k outlier lifts the mean $13.6k above the median. When someone quotes 'average salary', ask which average: medians describe the typical person; means describe the total pool. For negotiation anchoring, the median of comparable roles is the honest number.

