Worked: a certification costs $400 and 60 study hours. If it raises your market rate by $5/hour, break-even is 400/5 = **80** paid hours ≈ **2** work-weeks — ignoring the opportunity cost of study time. Add it: 60 hours × your current $40/hour = $2,400 forgone, so true cost $2,800 → break-even **{2800//5}** hours. Run this math before any paid credential or bootcamp: price ÷ hourly uplift, plus opportunity cost.

